WEBVTT

00:00:00.710 --> 00:00:09.750
<i>The countless flowers,
enveloped in light…</i>

00:00:09.750 --> 00:00:19.790
<i>…gaze at tomorrow
with unwavering eyes.</i>

00:00:32.340 --> 00:00:39.350
<i>Everyone wishes for me to be pure…</i>

00:00:39.350 --> 00:00:46.810
<i>…but what can I bring
with me to the frayed skies?</i>

00:00:46.810 --> 00:00:53.900
<i>What I’ve made my own
by breaking off flowers in bloom…</i>

00:00:53.900 --> 00:00:59.480
<i>All such sinful things…</i>

00:00:59.480 --> 00:01:06.950
<i>Why did I stop making
promises with the future?</i>

00:01:06.950 --> 00:01:14.220
<i>Because even if I try
to run far from all the pain…</i>

00:01:14.220 --> 00:01:20.930
<i>…a cold wind rustles
my hair… Don’t you see?</i>

00:01:20.930 --> 00:01:27.880
<i>Where can I ever find the answer?</i>

00:01:59.330 --> 00:02:01.510
Who are you? What are you doing?

00:02:01.510 --> 00:02:02.510
Oh my.

00:02:03.310 --> 00:02:04.770
How’d you get in here?

00:02:08.140 --> 00:02:11.550
The Simouns really
are nothing like Similes.

00:02:11.550 --> 00:02:14.480
I asked who you were.
Also, those clothes…

00:02:15.280 --> 00:02:19.450
Sorry, Waporif!
She’s one of our new recruits.

00:02:19.450 --> 00:02:22.630
Forgive me.
I didn’t know you were a sibylla.

00:02:22.630 --> 00:02:26.450
Not at all.
I should be apologizing to you.

00:02:27.290 --> 00:02:28.670
That’s Morinas.

00:02:28.670 --> 00:02:29.710
Yes.

00:02:32.130 --> 00:02:34.870
The helical motors
were discovered like this…

00:02:34.870 --> 00:02:38.420
…two spiral-shaped
devices always in pairs.

00:02:39.670 --> 00:02:42.940
And so that humans could
board and control them…

00:02:42.940 --> 00:02:46.540
…two cockpits and instrument
panels were added later.

00:02:46.540 --> 00:02:50.980
The collective term we
use for convenience is Simoun.

00:02:51.610 --> 00:02:52.980
Yes, that’s right.

00:02:55.880 --> 00:02:58.240
Most likely,
what’s controlling this side is…

00:02:58.690 --> 00:02:59.740
Most likely?

00:02:59.740 --> 00:03:03.490
Right. Most likely,
what’s controlling this side…

00:03:03.490 --> 00:03:08.010
…first existed in space. Perhaps
we should call it the power of space.

00:03:08.010 --> 00:03:13.450
And controlling the other side is what
we might call the power of time.

00:03:13.450 --> 00:03:16.020
That’s uncertain too?

00:03:16.020 --> 00:03:17.760
Yes, it is.

00:03:17.760 --> 00:03:21.990
Actually, we know almost
nothing about the helical motors…

00:03:21.990 --> 00:03:24.760
…that were excavated
from the earth’s depths.

00:03:24.760 --> 00:03:25.800
All we know…

00:03:25.800 --> 00:03:28.050
All we know…
…is how to operate them.

00:03:28.050 --> 00:03:34.000
We only maintain the sections
added on top of the helical motors.

00:03:34.000 --> 00:03:35.020
That’s the story.

00:03:35.800 --> 00:03:37.170
I see.

00:03:37.170 --> 00:03:42.740
But Simile Simouns were built based
on helical-motor research, right?

00:03:43.200 --> 00:03:48.870
Yes, but riding them till now, you know
the Similes’ capabilities best of all.

00:03:48.870 --> 00:03:53.250
Compared to Simouns,
Similes are just low-quality knockoffs.

00:03:53.250 --> 00:03:55.750
There’s no comparison.

00:03:55.750 --> 00:04:01.230
Oh, I’ve heard there’s no conclusive
data on the Simouns as of yet.

00:04:01.230 --> 00:04:03.010
It’s not good to hold back.

00:04:03.010 --> 00:04:04.260
Hold back?

00:04:04.930 --> 00:04:11.130
Simouns are holy vessels offered up
to Tempus Spatium in sacred rituals.

00:04:11.130 --> 00:04:13.640
We regard them accordingly.

00:04:13.640 --> 00:04:15.020
Exactly, Morinas.

00:04:15.540 --> 00:04:19.980
We are here to offer
the Ri Majon to Tempus Spatium.

00:04:19.980 --> 00:04:22.030
As priestesses
serving Tempus Spatium.

00:04:22.780 --> 00:04:24.740
I’m no priestess.

00:04:25.140 --> 00:04:27.240
Then what are you?

00:04:27.240 --> 00:04:31.880
I just want to fly a Simoun.
I’m not a priestess like you.

00:04:31.880 --> 00:04:32.710
But…

00:04:32.710 --> 00:04:33.500
But?

00:04:37.590 --> 00:04:41.260
I’m no soldier.
You’re not either, right, Paraietta?

00:04:43.990 --> 00:04:46.670
Oh, Paraietta. And you are?

00:04:46.670 --> 00:04:47.960
That’s Morinas, Floe.

00:04:47.960 --> 00:04:49.700
That’s Morinas, Floe.
Oh, right.

00:04:49.700 --> 00:04:53.530
It’s Morinas, right? Morinas…

00:04:53.970 --> 00:04:55.100
Good morning, Floe.

00:04:55.100 --> 00:04:58.080
Good morning, Floe.
Jeez, I just can’t remember names.

00:04:58.080 --> 00:04:59.730
And besides…

00:05:01.440 --> 00:05:07.030
Sorry. When I first saw you, I thought
you were Waporif’s new girlfriend.

00:05:08.080 --> 00:05:10.030
That couldn’t be.

00:05:12.490 --> 00:05:15.700
My windshield’s twisted.
I want it looked at.

00:05:15.700 --> 00:05:17.000
Understood!

00:05:17.730 --> 00:05:22.800
In the afternoon, I want more details of
the Similes and Simouns’ differences.

00:05:22.800 --> 00:05:26.240
I’ll be happy to.
Not just with the Simouns…

00:05:26.240 --> 00:05:30.050
If you ever need to, you can
ask us anything about this ship.

00:05:30.550 --> 00:05:31.770
Thank you.

00:05:36.810 --> 00:05:38.900
Wait. I’ll go with you.

00:05:39.250 --> 00:05:42.020
So was that helpful, Morinas?

00:05:42.020 --> 00:05:45.400
I wonder if I’ll learn
something new this afternoon.

00:05:47.910 --> 00:05:53.910
<b>The Distant War</b>

00:07:40.230 --> 00:07:41.390
Neviril…

00:07:41.390 --> 00:07:45.310
I am grateful that you’ve
returned from the Spring.

00:07:45.310 --> 00:07:51.420
I assume this means you’ve chosen
to continue on as a Simoun sibylla?

00:07:51.420 --> 00:07:54.660
I am still not certain. Besides…

00:07:55.080 --> 00:07:56.120
Besides?

00:07:57.050 --> 00:07:59.930
I am currently without a pair.

00:07:59.930 --> 00:08:02.620
Still, you have returned.

00:08:08.880 --> 00:08:11.590
Huh? What are you guys doing?

00:08:12.040 --> 00:08:13.590
You’re late, Aer.

00:08:13.590 --> 00:08:16.300
Oh, right. Sorry, sorry.

00:08:18.140 --> 00:08:19.690
For what?

00:08:19.690 --> 00:08:23.560
Our ceremony where we gather
in the ballroom after breakfast.

00:08:23.560 --> 00:08:27.560
Oh, the one from when
the chor was on graveyard shift?

00:08:27.560 --> 00:08:33.340
Anyway, would you like to have
a maju session in the pool at 3 PM?

00:08:35.760 --> 00:08:37.270
All of us?

00:08:37.270 --> 00:08:39.080
This is compulsory?

00:08:39.460 --> 00:08:40.510
Yes.

00:08:40.510 --> 00:08:42.440
At 3 PM?

00:08:42.440 --> 00:08:46.330
It’s a good idea. Let’s do it.
Since we’re all a little…

00:08:49.400 --> 00:08:51.980
We have lost three comrades.

00:08:51.980 --> 00:08:55.340
And afterwards,
three more left for the Spring.

00:08:55.780 --> 00:08:59.760
And in this emergency,
we’ve been relieved of night duties.

00:08:59.760 --> 00:09:01.350
We were the elite.

00:09:01.890 --> 00:09:05.430
As priestesses and as sibyllae.

00:09:05.430 --> 00:09:07.760
We’ll regain our glory.

00:09:07.760 --> 00:09:09.360
I’d like to.

00:09:09.360 --> 00:09:14.100
I just joined, so being in
a maju with an active chor is nice.

00:09:14.100 --> 00:09:17.370
So you’re saying to do this at 3 PM?

00:09:17.370 --> 00:09:20.120
Hey, what’s this
about 3 PM anyway?

00:09:20.120 --> 00:09:21.960
That’s when…

00:09:30.090 --> 00:09:34.500
3 PM is always Neviril’s maju time.

00:09:39.340 --> 00:09:41.560
Sibylla Aurea Neviril.

00:09:41.560 --> 00:09:43.470
I am honored to meet you.

00:09:44.300 --> 00:09:45.370
And you’re…

00:09:45.370 --> 00:09:50.270
I just joined the most
powerful chor… Chor Tempest.

00:09:50.270 --> 00:09:51.320
This is Morinas.

00:09:53.650 --> 00:09:57.430
I see. Please try to get
along with the others.

00:10:02.210 --> 00:10:05.750
Aer, you team up with Morinas.

00:10:06.850 --> 00:10:09.750
I thought I was paired with you.

00:10:09.750 --> 00:10:13.500
Don’t be so arrogant just
because you were once.

00:10:13.500 --> 00:10:17.050
First of all, no one thinks
you’re capable of replacing Amuria…

00:10:17.590 --> 00:10:20.100
That’s enough, Paraietta.

00:10:20.100 --> 00:10:21.730
Excuse me…

00:10:21.730 --> 00:10:25.270
We’re all gathering at
the pool at 3 PM for a maju.

00:10:25.270 --> 00:10:26.580
Oh?

00:10:26.580 --> 00:10:30.710
That’s when you always have
a maju, right, Sibylla Aurea?

00:10:30.710 --> 00:10:34.540
If your pair for that isn’t
set yet, please choose me.

00:10:36.710 --> 00:10:42.320
Morinas, maju pairs are always
determined by the natural flow.

00:10:42.320 --> 00:10:44.530
It’s not set in advance.

00:10:44.530 --> 00:10:48.540
I would be honored to pair up
with you, Sibylla Aurea.

00:10:49.490 --> 00:10:50.720
I see.

00:11:21.530 --> 00:11:27.040
Don’t worry. That won’t inflict
any real damage to the Arcus Prima.

00:11:27.040 --> 00:11:29.100
Y-Yes, ma’am.

00:11:29.100 --> 00:11:33.040
You are proud candidates
for the Simoun sibylla post.

00:11:33.040 --> 00:11:35.270
Hold your heads higher.

00:11:35.270 --> 00:11:36.600
Yes, ma’am.

00:11:45.150 --> 00:11:48.060
That’s more than usual,
don’t you think?

00:11:48.060 --> 00:11:50.560
Maybe we should go out too…

00:11:51.150 --> 00:11:52.390
I want to.

00:11:52.390 --> 00:11:55.390
We’re off combat duty right now.

00:12:27.820 --> 00:12:30.470
They’re showering more
greetings than usual today.

00:12:30.930 --> 00:12:34.340
Such long-distance tactics
are just harassment…

00:12:34.340 --> 00:12:36.810
…but the damage isn’t zero.

00:12:36.810 --> 00:12:39.980
I’ve been thinking
I’d like to take care of this.

00:12:41.140 --> 00:12:43.990
Is Chor Tempest finished?

00:12:44.400 --> 00:12:47.850
We can make up
for the losses somehow.

00:12:47.850 --> 00:12:49.250
Neviril?

00:12:49.250 --> 00:12:52.550
Yes. No matter what the remedy…

00:12:52.550 --> 00:12:57.000
…unless she returns,
Chor Tempest will remain scattered.

00:13:12.600 --> 00:13:14.340
You’re early, Aer.

00:13:14.340 --> 00:13:16.020
You too, Alty.

00:13:16.770 --> 00:13:19.150
It’s still a half hour till 3 PM!

00:13:23.150 --> 00:13:25.200
So you’re here, Big Sister.

00:13:28.450 --> 00:13:31.900
I stopped by your room to pick you up.

00:13:31.900 --> 00:13:35.590
If you’re sisters,
why don’t you fly a Simoun together?

00:13:35.590 --> 00:13:40.690
Being sisters has nothing to do with
the chemistry of auriga and sagitta.

00:13:40.690 --> 00:13:41.920
You tried?

00:13:42.960 --> 00:13:44.420
It’s clear enough without trying.

00:13:46.040 --> 00:13:47.930
I shouldn’t have asked.

00:13:55.710 --> 00:13:59.440
When this ship was a private
cruiser for observing Ri Majons…

00:13:59.440 --> 00:14:01.940
…it must’ve been a sight.

00:14:02.880 --> 00:14:07.450
But now it’s been overhauled into
a battle mother ship for Simoun chors.

00:14:08.130 --> 00:14:11.430
No more gentlemen and
ladies coming and going…

00:14:11.430 --> 00:14:14.840
Even on this beautiful
afternoon bathed in light…

00:14:14.840 --> 00:14:20.170
…there’s no one gathered before the
gigantic central ballroom except us.

00:14:20.170 --> 00:14:21.840
Just the three of us.

00:14:24.600 --> 00:14:29.470
I don’t want it to change like this.

00:14:37.480 --> 00:14:41.230
It looks so fun! I can’t stand it!

00:14:41.230 --> 00:14:43.530
Can’t I fly this now?

00:14:43.530 --> 00:14:46.900
Simouns can’t fly with
one pilot, unlike Similes.

00:14:46.900 --> 00:14:50.170
It needs one more
person aboard, your pair.

00:14:50.170 --> 00:14:51.490
That’s right.

00:14:53.400 --> 00:14:58.820
Helical motors activate when they
receive Tempus Spatium’s grace.

00:14:58.820 --> 00:15:05.020
But if either the auriga or sagitta
is missing, it can’t receive this grace.

00:15:05.020 --> 00:15:07.960
Both members of
the pair must be aboard.

00:15:07.960 --> 00:15:10.890
Hey, can I ask you something?

00:15:10.890 --> 00:15:11.970
Sure, what is it?

00:15:13.360 --> 00:15:15.970
When did you go
to the Spring, Waporif?

00:15:16.600 --> 00:15:19.520
Two years and
four months ago, I think?

00:15:19.930 --> 00:15:24.410
When I met Floe this morning, there
was a strange tension with you two.

00:15:24.410 --> 00:15:28.510
Oh, actually, Floe and I
used to be in love.

00:15:28.510 --> 00:15:30.490
I-In love?

00:15:30.970 --> 00:15:35.850
Inappropriate with a Simoun sibylla,
the symbol of utmost respect, right?

00:15:35.850 --> 00:15:38.160
No, that’s not what I meant.

00:15:40.180 --> 00:15:42.920
But it is a little awkward now.

00:15:52.460 --> 00:15:55.470
You’re going to the pool, aren’t you?

00:15:55.470 --> 00:15:58.430
I told you. I’m not
going to join in the maju.

00:15:59.100 --> 00:16:01.010
I won’t choose anyone.

00:16:01.010 --> 00:16:02.330
But…

00:16:02.740 --> 00:16:03.700
What?

00:16:04.300 --> 00:16:10.120
What happened to Amuria was tragic.
She was a dear comrade to us too.

00:16:10.120 --> 00:16:15.100
After that, I think I understand why
some of us headed for the Spring.

00:16:28.060 --> 00:16:30.670
Neviril, more… More powerful, Neviril.

00:16:31.410 --> 00:16:34.630
Neviril, don’t look! You can’t
kill them if you see their eyes!

00:17:40.930 --> 00:17:44.980
Listen, Morinas.
Any pairing is allowed in the pool.

00:17:44.980 --> 00:17:47.540
You don’t have to think
about your battle partner.

00:17:48.180 --> 00:17:52.050
So it’s first come, first served.
Pair up with whomever you like…

00:17:57.320 --> 00:18:00.050
Maybe Neviril won’t
come if we’re here.

00:18:02.060 --> 00:18:05.840
A maju without Neviril
won’t be much practice.

00:18:05.840 --> 00:18:07.060
I’m sure…

00:18:09.100 --> 00:18:10.560
I’m sure she’ll come.

00:18:10.560 --> 00:18:13.770
I guess that’s too bad, Paraietta.

00:18:20.910 --> 00:18:23.980
Maybe Neviril won’t come after all?

00:18:23.980 --> 00:18:26.080
Shall I call her?

00:18:26.080 --> 00:18:29.170
You shouldn’t say
things you’re not capable of.

00:18:30.450 --> 00:18:33.420
Even though she went to
the Spring, Neviril came back.

00:18:34.920 --> 00:18:40.740
That means she decided to remain
a Simoun sibylla of her own will, right?

00:18:40.740 --> 00:18:42.710
Yes, that’s right.

00:18:42.710 --> 00:18:44.590
Then she will come.

00:19:33.810 --> 00:19:37.820
What are you doing?
Floe, concentrate harder!

00:19:37.820 --> 00:19:38.820
Damn.

00:20:12.620 --> 00:20:16.520
With these scattered emotions,
we can’t achieve a maju.

00:20:17.490 --> 00:20:20.610
Even us, Chor Tempest…

00:20:22.560 --> 00:20:23.940
I don’t know…

00:20:23.940 --> 00:20:27.120
I think you’re jumping
to conclusions a little too fast.

00:20:41.710 --> 00:20:42.760
Neviril…

00:20:58.900 --> 00:21:02.280
Are you there?

00:21:09.410 --> 00:21:10.490
Are you?

00:22:09.720 --> 00:22:11.470
Hurry!

00:22:12.810 --> 00:22:16.750
No matter how hard
you try to protect them…

00:22:16.750 --> 00:22:18.230
…this is the reality.

00:22:24.020 --> 00:22:26.760
I’ll… I’ll get you out right now!

00:22:26.760 --> 00:22:27.990
Fire unit, hurry!

00:22:41.130 --> 00:22:47.850
<i>It is played by my wounds…
the song of prayer.</i>

00:22:47.850 --> 00:22:52.080
<i>Let it ring out over
the grieving universe.</i>

00:22:52.080 --> 00:22:59.120
<i>Can we change tomorrow?
Don’t be afraid.</i>

00:22:59.120 --> 00:23:06.750
<i>I want to let you know
how my heart’s overflowing.</i>

00:23:15.570 --> 00:23:19.640
<i>“I want to get closer to you.”
“I want to feel your pulse.”</i>

00:23:19.640 --> 00:23:24.820
<i>I was too defiant,
and I took the long way around.</i>

00:23:24.820 --> 00:23:28.830
<i>The blue moon is swaying silently.</i>

00:23:28.830 --> 00:23:32.800
<i>My true heart’s desire is you.</i>

00:23:32.800 --> 00:23:38.700
<i>I can’t reach you.
My tears of pain trickle down.</i>

00:23:38.700 --> 00:23:44.240
<i>Soar away into the sky, song of prayer.</i>

00:23:44.240 --> 00:23:47.680
<i>Carrying my love that came too late.</i>

00:23:47.680 --> 00:23:53.340
<i>What can I do to change tomorrow?</i>

00:23:53.340 --> 00:23:59.510
<i>Just hold on to “now” the way it is…</i>

00:24:04.960 --> 00:24:06.590
<b>To Be Continued</b>

00:24:08.150 --> 00:24:11.340
Rimone! Get a move on! Let’s go!

00:24:13.930 --> 00:24:15.470
Next time on Simoun…

00:24:15.470 --> 00:24:19.970
<b>The Nearby War</b>

00:24:16.160 --> 00:24:17.890
The Nearby War.
